he catalog''s Identify Plants & Fruit, 25+15 = 40. Land Navigation 36+15 = 51. Track Animals is the catalog''s Track & Trap Animals, 20+15 = 35. Skin & Prepare Animal Hides 30+15 = 45. Wilderness Survival 30+20 = 50. Hand to Hand: Expert with no upgrade price printed, so no hand_to_hand block. Climb 95%/90% is printed under natural abilities and stored as Climbing 95 with per_level 0 (judgement: the book prints a fixed figure and no per-level step; the second figure, 90%, is in the note). || RONII: the one tribe with its own printed skills is the ronii variant; the class with no variant is a Tokae or Kreenae warrior. Horsemanship is the catalog''s Horsemanship: General, 40+30 = 70; Horsemanship: Exotic Animals 30+30 = 60. The Ronii''s wider skill selection (any Communications, Military, Piloting and Rogue), the horse or exotic riding animal and the choice of another O.C.C. are restriction text. || RELATED: four at level one, plus one at levels 2, 5, 8 and 12. Domestic +10, Medical (First Aid and Holistic Medicine only) +5, Rogue +5, Technical +5, Wilderness +10; Electrical, Mechanical, Military, Pilot Related and Science none. Scrambler is Radio: Scramblers. ''Pilot: Truck, Hovercraft and horsemanship only'' is Pilot limited to Truck and Hover Craft (ground) plus the catalog''s Horsemanship category limited to Horsemanship: General and Horsemanship: Exotic Animals (judgement: the other Horsemanship rows are styles of named occupations). SECONDARY: four at level one plus one at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12, same lists without bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: survival knife or hatchet as a choice; ''one or two Vibro-Blades'' as a choice of one blade with the printed count in the note; the energy rifle is printed without a model and stored as a choice among four catalog rifles; 1D4 E-clips; knapsack, utility belt, air filter, two canteens. || MONEY: the book prints no starting sum; no starting_money stored. || Population, tribal ranges, disposition, allies and enemies, and additional equipment are lore."
